      "marks": 4,
      "chapter": "Calculus",
      "topic": "Definite integrals and area",
      "question": "Evaluate the definite integral $\\displaystyle\\int_1^{2} 3x^2 \\, dx$.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "$7$", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "$9$", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "$8$", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "$3$", "is_correct": false}
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "$7$",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Antiderivative: $\\int 3x^2\\,dx = x^3$.",
          "Apply limits: $[x^3]_1^2 = 2^3 - 1^3 = 8 - 1 = 7$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["integral of x^n = x^{n+1}/(n+1)"],
        "commonMistake": "Forgetting to subtract the value at the lower limit.",
        "examinerNote": "Fundamental theorem of calculus."
      },
      "verification": {"kind": "symbolic_integral_def", "integrand": "3*x**2", "lower": 1, "upper": 2, "expected": 7},
      "tags": ["numerical", "calculus"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "Numerical",
      "difficulty": "Board",
      "bloomLevel": "Apply",
      "marks": 3,
      "chapter": "Calculus",
      "topic": "Definite integrals and area",
      "question": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{4} x \\, dx$ and report the numerical value.",
      "numericAnswer": 8,
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "$8$",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Antiderivative: $\\int x\\,dx = x^2/2$.",
          "Apply limits: $[x^2/2]_0^4 = 16/2 - 0 = 8$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["integral of x = x^2/2"],
        "commonMistake": "Dividing by the wrong constant or skipping the lower limit.",
        "examinerNote": "Equals the area of a triangle of base 4 and height 4."
      },
      "verification": {"kind": "symbolic_integral_def", "integrand": "x", "lower": 0, "upper": 4, "expected": 8},
      "tags": ["numerical", "board"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "SCQ",
      "difficulty": "JEE_Main",
      "bloomLevel": "Apply",
      "marks": 4,
      "chapter": "Vectors and 3D Geometry",
      "topic": "Scalar (dot) product",
      "question": "For $\\vec{a} = \\hat{i} + 2\\hat{j} + 2\\hat{k}$ and $\\vec{b} = 2\\hat{i} + 0\\hat{j} + \\hat{k}$, the scalar product $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b}$ is:",
      "options": [
        {"text": "$4$", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "$2$", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "$6$", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "$8$", "is_correct": false}
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "$4$",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Dot product: $\\vec{a}\\cdot\\vec{b} = a_x b_x + a_y b_y + a_z b_z$.",
          "$= (1)(2) + (2)(0) + (2)(1) = 2 + 0 + 2 = 4$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["a.b = ax bx + ay by + az bz"],
        "commonMistake": "Adding components instead of multiplying matching components.",
        "examinerNote": "The dot product is a scalar."
      },
      "verification": {"kind": "numeric", "expression": "1*2 + 2*0 + 2*1", "expected": 4, "tol": 0.0001},
      "tags": ["numerical", "vectors"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "Numerical",
      "difficulty": "JEE_Advanced",
      "bloomLevel": "Apply",
      "marks": 4,
      "chapter": "Vectors and 3D Geometry",
      "topic": "Vector (cross) product",
      "question": "Two vectors are mutually perpendicular with $|\\vec{a}| = 2$ and $|\\vec{b}| = 3$. Find $|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|$.",
      "numericAnswer": 6,
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "$6$",
        "stepByStep": [
          "$|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}| = |\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\sin\\theta$.",
          "Perpendicular: $\\theta = 90^\\circ$, $\\sin\\theta = 1$.",
          "$|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}| = 2 \\times 3 \\times 1 = 6$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["|a x b| = |a||b| sin(theta)"],
        "commonMistake": "Using $\\cos\\theta$ (that is the dot product).",
        "examinerNote": "Equals the area of the parallelogram formed by the vectors."
      },
      "verification": {"kind": "numeric", "expression": "2*3", "expected": 6, "tol": 0.0001},
      "tags": ["numerical", "vectors"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "SCQ",
      "difficulty": "JEE_Main",
      "bloomLevel": "Apply",
      "marks": 4,
      "chapter": "Probability",
      "topic": "Binomial distribution",
      "question": "A fair coin is tossed $4$ times. The probability of getting exactly $2$ heads is:",
      "options": [
        {"text": "$0.375$", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "$0.25$", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "$0.5$", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "$0.125$", "is_correct": false}
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "$0.375$ (i.e. $3/8$)",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Binomial: $P(X=k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$ with $n=4$, $p=0.5$.",
          "$P(X=2) = \\binom{4}{2}(0.5)^4 = 6 \\times 0.0625 = 0.375$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["P(X=k) = C(n,k) p^k (1-p)^{n-k}"],
        "commonMistake": "Forgetting the $\\binom{4}{2} = 6$ combinatorial factor.",
        "examinerNote": "Each toss is independent with $p = 0.5$."
      },
      "verification": {"kind": "numeric", "expression": "6*(0.5**4)", "expected": 0.375, "tol": 0.0001},
      "tags": ["numerical", "probability"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "MCQ",
      "difficulty": "JEE_Advanced",
      "bloomLevel": "Analyze",
      "marks": 4,
      "chapter": "Vectors and 3D Geometry",
      "topic": "Vector (cross) product",
      "question": "Select ALL correct statements about the cross product $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}$.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "It is anti-commutative: $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = -(\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{a})$.", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "Its magnitude equals the area of the parallelogram formed by $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$.", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "It is the zero vector when $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are parallel.", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "The result is a scalar quantity.", "is_correct": false}
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "Statements 1, 2 and 3 are correct.",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Swapping the order flips the direction: $\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = -(\\vec{b}\\times\\vec{a})$.",
          "$|\\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b}|$ is the parallelogram area.",
          "Parallel vectors give $\\sin\\theta = 0$, so the product is the zero vector.",
          "The result is a VECTOR, not a scalar, so the last statement is false."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["|a x b| = |a||b| sin(theta)"],
        "commonMistake": "Treating the cross product like the dot product (which gives a scalar).",
        "examinerNote": "Direction follows the right-hand rule."
      },
      "tags": ["multiple-correct", "vectors"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "AssertionReason",
      "difficulty": "JEE_Main",
      "bloomLevel": "Understand",
      "marks": 4,
      "chapter": "Calculus",
      "topic": "Differentiation and applications of derivatives",
      "question": "Assertion (A): $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\sin x) = \\cos x$.\nReason (R): From first principles, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sin x = \\lim_{h\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin(x+h)-\\sin x}{h}$, which simplifies to $\\cos x$ using $\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sin h}{h}=1$.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A.", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "A is true but R is false.", "is_correct": false},
        {"text": "A is false but R is true.", "is_correct": false}
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "Both A and R are true and R correctly explains A.",
        "stepByStep": [
          "Expand $\\sin(x+h) = \\sin x\\cos h + \\cos x\\sin h$.",
          "The difference quotient becomes $\\sin x\\frac{\\cos h - 1}{h} + \\cos x\\frac{\\sin h}{h}$.",
          "As $h\\to0$: $\\frac{\\cos h - 1}{h}\\to 0$ and $\\frac{\\sin h}{h}\\to 1$, giving $\\cos x$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["d/dx sin x = cos x"],
        "commonMistake": "Quoting the result without recognising it follows from the standard limit.",
        "examinerNote": "R is precisely the derivation of A."
      },
      "tags": ["assertion-reason", "calculus"]
    },
    {
      "questionType": "TF",
      "difficulty": "Board",
      "bloomLevel": "Understand",
      "marks": 1,
      "chapter": "Probability",
      "topic": "Conditional probability and independence",
      "question": "State whether True or False: If $A$ and $B$ are independent events with $P(B) > 0$, then $P(A\\mid B) = P(A)$.",
      "options": [
        {"text": "True", "is_correct": true},
        {"text": "False", "is_correct": false}
      ],
      "solution": {
        "finalAnswer": "True",
        "stepByStep": [
          "$P(A\\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(A\\cap B)}{P(B)}$.",
          "Independence: $P(A\\cap B) = P(A)P(B)$.",
          "So $P(A\\mid B) = \\dfrac{P(A)P(B)}{P(B)} = P(A)$."
        ],
        "formulaUsed": ["P(A|B) = P(A and B)/P(B)", "independence: P(A and B) = P(A)P(B)"],
        "commonMistake": "Confusing independent events with mutually exclusive ones.",
        "examinerNote": "Independence means $B$ gives no information about $A$."
      },
      "tags": ["true-false", "probability"]
    }
  ]
}
